[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch_dist_1_1
diagnosis_text:
The failure is in the Layer-3/routing subsystem on the distribution switch for pod 1 (switch_dist_1_1), not the access switch. Host 10.1.1.2 (host_1_1_1_1) has a correct IP/gateway and can ARP its default gateway (10.1.1.1). From the host, pings to external networks return “Destination Net Unreachable” generated by 10.1.1.1, proving the default gateway itself lacks routes beyond the local subnet.

On switch_dist_1_1, the routing table contains only connected networks (10.1.1.0/24 on br0 and 172.16.0.6/31 on eth0), and FRR/OSPF is not running: “ospfd is not running” and systemd shows “frr.service … Active: failed (failed).” In contrast, switch_dist_2_1 has FRR running and OSPF routes installed to the server farm (10.200.0.0/24) and core subnets. The access switch (switch_access_1_1_1) is purely L2 bridging to the distribution switch, and the L2 path is healthy (switch_dist_1_1 can ping host_1_1_1_1 successfully; host ARP shows 10.1.1.1 learned).

Root cause: FRR (OSPF) is down on switch_dist_1_1, so no dynamic routes are present, and it correctly returns ICMP net-unreachable for all off-subnet destinations.

Corrective fix: Do not replace the access switch. Restore routing on switch_dist_1_1 by restarting and fixing FRR (e.g., systemctl restart frr; ensure /etc/frr/daemons enables ospfd and frr.conf is valid). After FRR is running, OSPF will install routes to the core/server networks and host_1_1_1_1 connectivity will be restored. If hardware replacement is considered, replace switch_dist_1_1, not the access switch.
=== END ===